    "body": "Fixes #4477\n\n## Problem\n\nForeground `type_text` (and `press_key`) restored the previously active window a fixed 40 ms after `SendInput`. Editors that process Return slowly (Notepad, WPF/WinUI3 multiline TextBoxes) had not yet consumed the queued tail, so text after a line break was dropped or delivered elsewhere (#4477).\n\n## Fix\n\n`with_confirmed_foreground` (`platform-windows/src/input/keyboard.rs`) now attaches to the foreground thread's input queue before inserting anything, appends a harmless sentinel key (unassigned VK `0xE8`) after the input, and restores the previous foreground only after the target thread has read it. The `GetKeyState` toggle bit on the shared queue shows this. The wait is bounded at 2 s, and if attaching fails it falls back to the previous 40 ms settle.\n\n## Tests (by @wszkxlllll)\n\n- WPF and WinUI3 fixtures gain a dedicated multiline `TextBox` and publish their control text to an app-owned, atomically replaced state file (`CUA_E2E_FIXTURE_STATE_PATH`).\n- New harness tests cover foreground single-line text (CJK, digits, emoji) and multiline text (LF, CR, CRLF, repeated blank lines, leading/trailing breaks), compared against the app-owned state with line endings normalized, plus leak checks on sibling inputs.\n- A/B on `E2E: Rust Windows interactive` (native lane): main loses text after line breaks in both frameworks ([run](https://github.com/trycua/cua/actions/runs/37106385663)). With the drain fix, the full native lane passes, including these tests and the WPF accelerator test ([run](https://github.com/trycua/cua/actions/runs/37109218138)).\n\nThe earlier batching and admission rework on this branch was dropped by agreement after the A/B showed it did not change delivery; see the review thread.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Hv7NU2xZDx8fqykTXiaDuj\n",
